            <div xml:id="d855">

                <pb facs="0894" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860H.24/114</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Yugoslav Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fotitch</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-21">September 21, 1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of September 19, 1939, informing me that your Government
                    contemplates purchasing a large quantity of arms, ammunition, and implements of
                    war in the United States.</p>
                <p>I have taken due note of your assurance that these arms, ammunition, and
                    implements of war are intended solely for the use of the Yugoslav Army.</p>
                <p>Prompt consideration will be given to any application which the Department may
                    receive for licenses to export these arms, ammunition, and implements of
                    war.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Walton Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
